    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0189" n="94" xml:id="pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.943/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-01T12:00:00-05:00">April 1, 1936—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. Reference Dairen’s despatch of February 26 addressed to Embassy at
                        Tokyo<anchor n="27" xml:id="d82-f1"/> in regard to reported tariff agreement
                    between the authorities of the “autonomous” area of North China and those of
                    Japan.</p>
                <p>Department assumes that you are already studying the situation under reference
                    and that in due course you will inform the Department of the results of your
                        investigation.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d82-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d82-f1" n="27" xml:id="d82-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d82-f2" n="28" xml:id="d82-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 215, April 30, 11 a.m., from the Ambassador in China, <ref
                        target="#pg126">p. 126</ref>.</p>
            </note>
